-| Local or territory | Test the assigned contribution, direction, evidence, inherited obligations, imported assumptions, and recipient usability. Cover the obligations allocated to that unit, not only its headings. |
-| Boundary | Inspect the canonical rule or bounded shared question and both sides' relevant obligations together. Test local compliance with incompatible meaning, authority, identity, timing, ordering, commitment, failure, recovery, or compatibility. Include shared state/resources and implicit dependencies, not only APIs. |
